---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Code lab">
  <h1>Code lab</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="max-width:820px">Write actual Qiskit (Python) or OpenQASM 3 and run it on a little simulator in the browser. Each exercise has tests (like Microsoft's Quantum Katas), and if you get one of the usual wrong answers it tells you what probably happened. Your code is saved in your browser.</p>

  <div class="lab-layout">
    <nav class="card" aria-label="Exercises">
      <div class="eyebrow">Exercises</div>
      <ol id="ex-list" style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:.4rem 0 0"></ol>
    </nav>

    <section>
      <div class="card">
        <h2 id="ex-title" style="margin:0 0 .3rem"></h2>
        <p id="ex-brief" style="margin:.2rem 0"></p>
        <p class="small" id="ex-predict" style="color:var(--shaky);margin:.4rem 0 0"></p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.8rem;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center">
          <div class="guidance" role="group" aria-label="Language">
            <button type="button" data-lang="qiskit" aria-pressed="true">Python · Qiskit</button>
            <button type="button" data-lang="qasm" aria-pressed="false">OpenQASM 3</button>
          </div>
          <div class="btn-row" style="margin:0">
            <button class="btn" id="run" type="button">▶ Run <span class="small" style="opacity:.75">(Ctrl+Enter)</span></button>
            <button class="btn secondary small" id="reset" type="button">Reset code</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <label class="sr-only" for="editor">Code editor (Tab indents; press Esc then Tab to leave)</label>
        <textarea id="editor" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off"></textarea>
        <div id="errors" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Circuit</div>
          <div id="circuit" style="overflow-x:auto"></div>
          <div class="eyebrow" style="margin-top:1rem">Final state (before measurement)</div>
          <div id="state" class="small" style="font-family:var(--mono);line-height:1.9;word-break:break-word"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap">
            <div class="eyebrow">Histogram · 1,024 shots</div>
            <label class="small"><input type="checkbox" id="qiskit-order" checked /> Qiskit bit order (q0 on the right)</label>
          </div>
          <div id="hist"></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Tests</div>
          <div id="tests" aria-live="polite"><p class="muted small">Run your code to check it.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="eyebrow">Tutor</div>
          <div id="tutor" aria-live="polite"><p class="muted small">After a run I'll point out common mistakes. Stuck? Take a hint; each one reveals a bit more.</p></div>
          <div class="btn-row"><button class="btn small secondary" id="hint" type="button">Give me a hint</button><button class="btn small secondary" id="solution" type="button">Show a solution</button></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <details class="card" style="margin-top:1rem">
        <summary>Run it on a real IBM quantum computer</summary>
        <p>The browser simulator is perfect (no noise). Real hardware isn't, and seeing the difference is worth doing once your circuit passes.</p>
        <ol>
          <li>Create a free account at <a href="https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/" rel="noopener">IBM Quantum Platform</a>. The Open Plan gives a monthly allowance of free hardware time (check the current terms on their site), plenty for small circuits like these.</li>
          <li>Install Qiskit on your laptop: <code>pip install qiskit qiskit-ibm-runtime</code>.</li>
          <li>Save your API key once (never put it in a public repo):
<pre><code>from qiskit_ibm_runtime import QiskitRuntimeService
QiskitRuntimeService.save_account(channel="ibm_quantum_platform", token="YOUR_API_KEY")</code></pre></li>
          <li>Run your circuit:
<pre><code>from qiskit import QuantumCircuit
from qiskit.transpiler import generate_preset_pass_manager
from qiskit_ibm_runtime import QiskitRuntimeService, SamplerV2 as Sampler

qc = QuantumCircuit(2)
qc.h(0)
qc.cx(0, 1)
qc.measure_all()

service = QiskitRuntimeService()
backend = service.least_busy(operational=True, simulator=False)
isa = generate_preset_pass_manager(backend=backend, optimization_level=1).run(qc)
job = Sampler(mode=backend).run([isa], shots=1024)
print(job.result()[0].data.meas.get_counts())</code></pre></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="small muted">Expect a few percent of "impossible" outcomes like 01 and 10 for a Bell pair: that is gate and readout noise. API details change between Qiskit versions; if this snippet errors, check the <a href="https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides" rel="noopener">IBM Quantum docs</a>. Running hardware jobs straight from this website would need a small server (for example a Cloudflare Worker) to keep your API key secret; it's a possible later addition.</p>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
<style is:global>
  .lab-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 250px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 1.4rem; align-items: start; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .lab-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  #editor { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .92rem; min-height: 260px; margin-top: .8rem; line-height: 1.55; tab-size: 4; white-space: pre; }
  #ex-list button { width: 100%; text-align: left; background: none; border: 0; color: var(--muted); font: inherit; padding: .4rem .5rem; border-radius: 8px; cursor: pointer; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: .4rem; }
  #ex-list button:hover { background: var(--bg-3); color: var(--text); }
  #ex-list button[aria-current="true"] { background: var(--bg-3); color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
  .err { background: var(--warn-bg); border-left: 4px solid var(--shaky); padding: .5rem .8rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-top: .5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
  .test { display: flex; gap: .5rem; align-items: baseline; margin: .3rem 0; }
</style>
<script>
  import { EXERCISES } from '../data/exercises';
  import { parseQiskit, parseQasm, run, type Op } from '../lib/qparse';
  import { sample } from '../lib/sim';
  import { ketString } from '../lib/ui';
  import { load, save, logError } from '../lib/store';

  let lang: 'qiskit' | 'qasm' = load('codeLang', 'qiskit');
  let ex = EXERCISES.find((e) => e.id === (new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('ex') ?? load('codeEx', 'random-bit'))) ?? EXERCISES[0];
  let hintIx = 0;
  const passed: Record<string, boolean> = load('codePassed', {});
  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id)!;
  const editor = $('editor') as HTMLTextAreaElement;
  const key = () => `code:${ex.id}:${lang}`;

  function list() {
    $('ex-list').innerHTML = EXERCISES.map((e) => `<li><button type="button" data-id="${e.id}" aria-current="${e.id === ex.id}"><span>${e.title}</span><span>${passed[e.id] ? '✓' : ''}</span></button></li>`).join('');
    $('ex-list').querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => select(b.dataset.id!)));
  }
  function select(id: string) {
    ex = EXERCISES.find((e) => e.id === id)!; save('codeEx', id); hintIx = 0;
    $('ex-title').textContent = ex.title;
    $('ex-brief').innerHTML = ex.brief + (ex.lecture ? ` <a class="small" href="/lectures#l${ex.lecture}">(Lecture ${ex.lecture})</a>` : '');
    $('ex-predict').textContent = 'Predict first: ' + ex.predict;
    editor.value = load(key(), lang === 'qiskit' ? ex.qiskit : ex.qasm);
    ['errors', 'circuit', 'state', 'hist'].forEach((k) => ($(k).innerHTML = ''));
    $('tests').innerHTML = '<p class="muted small">Run your code to check it.</p>';
    $('tutor').innerHTML = '<p class="muted small">After a run I\'ll point out common mistakes. Stuck? Take a hint; each one reveals a bit more.</p>';
    list();
  }
  function setLang(l: 'qiskit' | 'qasm') {
    lang = l; save('codeLang', l);
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]').forEach((b) => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b.dataset.lang === l)));
    editor.value = load(key(), l === 'qiskit' ? ex.qiskit : ex.qasm);
  }

  function drawCircuit(n: number, ops: Op[]) {
    const cols: number[] = []; const depth = Array(n).fill(0);
    ops.forEach((o, i) => { const lo = Math.min(...o.q), hi = Math.max(...o.q); let d = 0; for (let k = lo; k <= hi; k++) d = Math.max(d, depth[k]); cols[i] = d; for (let k = lo; k <= hi; k++) depth[k] = d + 1; });
    const W = 56, H = 44, L = 46, width = L + Math.max(1, ...depth) * W + 30, height = n * H + 10;
    const y = (q: number) => 25 + q * H, x = (c: number) => L + c * W + W / 2;
    let s = `<svg viewBox="0 0 ${width} ${height}" width="${width}" height="${height}" role="img" aria-label="Circuit diagram">`;
    for (let q = 0; q < n; q++) s += `<line x1="${L - 8}" y1="${y(q)}" x2="${width - 10}" y2="${y(q)}" stroke="var(--muted)"/><text x="4" y="${y(q) + 5}" class="svg-text" font-size="13" font-family="var(--mono)">q${q}</text>`;
    const label = (o: Op) => o.g === 'sdg' ? 'S†' : o.g === 'tdg' ? 'T†' : o.g === 'p' ? 'P' : o.g.toUpperCase();
    ops.forEach((o, i) => {
      const cx = x(cols[i]);
      if (o.g === 'cx' || o.g === 'ccx') {
        const t = o.q[o.q.length - 1];
        s += `<line x1="${cx}" y1="${y(Math.min(...o.q))}" x2="${cx}" y2="${y(Math.max(...o.q))}" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/>`;
        o.q.slice(0, -1).forEach((q) => (s += `<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${y(q)}" r="5" fill="var(--accent)"/>`));
        s += `<circle cx="${cx}" cy="${y(t)}" r="11" fill="var(--bg-2)" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="${cx - 11}" y1="${y(t)}" x2="${cx + 11}" y2="${y(t)}" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><line x1="${cx}" y1="${y(t) - 11}" x2="${cx}" y2="${y(t) + 11}" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/>`;
      } else if (o.g === 'cz') {
        s += `<line x1="${cx}" y1="${y(o.q[0])}" x2="${cx}" y2="${y(o.q[1])}" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/><circle cx="${cx}" cy="${y(o.q[0])}" r="5" fill="var(--accent)"/><circle cx="${cx}" cy="${y(o.q[1])}" r="5" fill="var(--accent)"/>`;
      } else if (o.g === 'swap') {
        s += `<line x1="${cx}" y1="${y(o.q[0])}" x2="${cx}" y2="${y(o.q[1])}" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2"/>` + o.q.map((q) => `<text x="${cx - 7}" y="${y(q) + 6}" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="18">×</text>`).join('');
      } else {
        const lab = label(o);
        s += `<rect x="${cx - 17}" y="${y(o.q[0]) - 15}" width="34" height="30" rx="5" fill="var(--bg-3)" stroke="var(--accent)"/><text x="${cx}" y="${y(o.q[0]) + 5}" text-anchor="middle" class="svg-text" font-size="${lab.length > 2 ? 11 : 14}">${lab}</text>`;
        if (o.theta !== undefined) s += `<text x="${cx}" y="${y(o.q[0]) + 27}" text-anchor="middle" class="svg-muted" font-size="9">${o.theta.toFixed(2)}</text>`;
      }
    });
    $('circuit').innerHTML = s + '</svg>';
  }

  function runIt() {
    save(key(), editor.value);
    const parsed = lang === 'qiskit' ? parseQiskit(editor.value) : parseQasm(editor.value);
    $('errors').innerHTML = parsed.errors.map((e) => `<div class="err"><strong>Line ${e.line}:</strong> ${e.msg.replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>')}</div>`).join('');
    if (parsed.errors.length) { $('tests').innerHTML = '<p class="small">Fix the errors above, then run again.</p>'; return; }
    const st = run(parsed.n, parsed.ops);
    drawCircuit(parsed.n, parsed.ops);
    $('state').innerHTML = `|ψ⟩ = ${ketString(st.amps, parsed.n)}<br><span class="muted">labels in lecture order |q0 q1 …⟩</span>`;
    const counts = sample(st, 1024);
    const qOrder = ($('qiskit-order') as HTMLInputElement).checked;
    const keys = Object.keys(counts).sort();
    $('hist').innerHTML = keys.map((k) => {
      const shown = qOrder ? [...k].reverse().join('') : k;
      return `<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:4.5rem 1fr 3rem;gap:.5rem;align-items:center;margin:.3rem 0"><code>${shown}</code><div class="bar"><span style="width:${(counts[k] / 1024) * 100}%;background:var(--accent)"></span></div><span class="small">${counts[k]}</span></div>`;
    }).join('') + (parsed.n > 1 ? `<p class="small muted">${qOrder ? 'Qiskit prints qubit 0 as the RIGHTMOST bit, so |q0 q1⟩ = |10⟩ shows as "01". Untick to see lecture order.' : 'Lecture order: q0 is the leftmost bit.'}</p>` : '') + (parsed.measured ? '' : '<p class="small muted">(No measure in your code; the histogram shows what measuring every qubit at the end would give.)</p>');
    const results = ex.tests(st, parsed.ops, parsed.n);
    $('tests').innerHTML = results.length ? results.map((t) => `<div class="test"><span style="color:${t.pass ? 'var(--good)' : 'var(--bad)'}">${t.pass ? '✓' : '✗'}</span><span>${t.name}</span></div>`).join('') + (results.every((t) => t.pass) ? '<p><strong>All tests pass.</strong> Try the other language, or explain to yourself why it works.</p>' : '') : '<p class="small muted">Sandbox: no tests.</p>';
    const ok = results.length > 0 && results.every((t) => t.pass);
    if (ok && !passed[ex.id]) { passed[ex.id] = true; save('codePassed', passed); list(); }
    const d = !ok ? ex.diagnose?.(st, parsed.ops) : null;
    if (d) { logError('code:' + ex.id); }
    $('tutor').innerHTML = d ? `<div class="callout mistake" style="margin:0"><div class="callout-title">What probably went wrong</div>${d}</div>` : ok ? '<p>That works.</p>' : results.length ? '<p class="small">Not there yet. Compare the final state with what the exercise asks for, or take a hint.</p>' : '';
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-lang]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => setLang(b.dataset.lang as 'qiskit' | 'qasm')));
  $('run').addEventListener('click', runIt);
  $('qiskit-order').addEventListener('change', runIt);
  $('reset').addEventListener('click', () => { editor.value = lang === 'qiskit' ? ex.qiskit : ex.qasm; save(key(), editor.value); });
  $('hint').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const h = ex.hints[Math.min(hintIx, ex.hints.length - 1)]; hintIx++;
    $('tutor').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `<p class="small"><strong>Hint ${Math.min(hintIx, ex.hints.length)}:</strong> ${h.replace(/`([^`]+)`/g, '<code>$1</code>')}</p>`);
  });
  $('solution').addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (!ex.solution) return;
    const body = lang === 'qiskit' ? ex.solution : ex.solution.replace(/qc\.(\w+)\(([^)]*)\)/g, (_m, g, a) => { const parts = a.split(',').map((x: string) => x.trim()); const isAngle = ['rx', 'ry', 'rz', 'p'].includes(g); return isAngle ? `${g}(${parts[0]}) q[${parts[1]}];` : `${g} ${parts.map((p: string) => `q[${p}]`).join(', ')};`; });
    $('tutor').insertAdjacentHTML('beforeend', `<p class="small"><strong>One solution</strong> (add after the setup lines):</p><pre><code>${body}</code></pre><p class="small muted">Type it yourself rather than pasting; it sticks better.</p>`);
  });
  // Tab indents inside the editor; press Esc first to move focus on with Tab (keyboard users).
  let trapTab = true;
  editor.addEventListener('focus', () => (trapTab = true));
  editor.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
    if (e.key === 'Escape') { trapTab = false; return; }
    if (e.key === 'Tab' && trapTab && !e.shiftKey) { e.preventDefault(); const s = editor.selectionStart; editor.setRangeText('    ', s, editor.selectionEnd, 'end'); }
    if (e.key === 'Enter' && (e.ctrlKey || e.metaKey)) { e.preventDefault(); runIt(); }
  });
  editor.addEventListener('input', () => save(key(), editor.value));
  setLang(lang);
  select(ex.id);
</script>
